# Implementation Log — 2026-11-04

## 01:00 - Direct File Delivery & PDF.js Regression Fix
- Root Cause: Flask was proxying raw Cloudinary PDF bytes, Service Worker was intercepting 206 byte ranges, and image papers (.jpg/.webp) were fed to PDF.js.
- Changes:
  - `routes/api.py`: Implemented `/api/documents/<doc_id>/authorize`, extension checking (`is_image`).
  - `routes/library.py`: Set `direct_pdf_url`, retained raw cloud delivery.
  - `templates/resource.html`: Updated lines 1124, 1166, 1208 to render direct signed URLs in PDF.js iframe and native Image Viewer for image papers.
  - `static/sw.js`: Bumped to `v2.0.13`, added `skipWaiting()` and `clients.claim()`, bypassed cross-origin requests.

## 01:30 - Client IndexedDB Delta Sync Store
- Changes:
  - `static/js/idb-sync-store.js`: Built `AbhiHubDataStore` caching `colleges`, `subjects`, `files`, `user_meta`.
  - `routes/api.py`: Added `/api/sync/versions` lightweight hashing endpoint.
  - Tested with headless Microsoft Edge: verified colleges and subjects populated; account-switch isolation clears user history while retaining catalogs.

